# Command Safety Rules

## Allowed without asking

Agents may run:

- npm run lint
- npm run build
- npm run check
- npx tsc --noEmit
- git status
- git status --short --untracked-files=all
- git diff
- git diff --stat
- git diff --name-only
- git log --oneline -5
- git branch --show-current

Read-only command chains are allowed only when every command is listed above.

## Allowed normal edits

Agents may directly edit/create files within approved scope:

- app files for approved routes
- components files for approved features
- lib files for approved helpers/store/mock data
- types files for approved domain models
- docs files
- .cursor/rules files
- .claude/agents files

## Ask before

Always ask before:

- npm install
- dependency updates
- modifying package.json
- changing lockfiles intentionally
- git add
- git commit
- git push
- git checkout
- git merge
- git rebase
- git reset
- git clean
- deleting major folders
- destructive shell commands
- changing .env files
- database migrations against real Supabase
- Vercel deploys
- production/staging changes
- broad architecture renames
- replacing the LocalOps modular foundation

## Never do silently

- Do not expose service role keys.
- Do not add API keys to source files.
- Do not commit secrets.
- Do not run destructive cleanup commands without approval.
